# Capacitor / Android apps (android-student, android-outlet)
# Gradle build output, local.properties and the generated capacitor.config.json
# are already covered by each app's own android/.gitignore, which Capacitor
# generates and we commit. Only what those files miss belongs here.
node_modules/
# Capacitor ships these two commented out; signing keys must never be committed.
*.keystore
*.jks
keystore.properties

# The Firebase *service account* key, which FcmSender reads to send FCM messages. This is
# a real secret: it can send notifications as this project.
firebase-service-account*.json
serviceAccountKey*.json
*-firebase-adminsdk-*.json

# Firebase client config. Not a secret in Google's sense — it ships inside every APK, so
# anyone with the app already has it — but this repository is public and no workflow here
# builds the Android apps, so publishing the project id and API key to scrapers buys
# nothing and invites quota abuse. Each developer drops their own copy in locally; see
# docs/android-apps.md.
google-services.json
